    name="3 Data Editing and Enrichment Value Stream"
    id="id-7eace385d7574bc389044438d062c8a5"
    documentation="Purpose:&#xD;&#xA;To improve the accuracy, completeness, and internal consistency of datasets through validation, correction, and enrichment processes.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Description:&#xD;&#xA;At this stage, value is created by enhancing data reliability and usability. Activities include error detection, imputation of missing data, derivation of new variables, and correction of inconsistencies or non-response. The goal is to maximize the analytical value of the dataset while maintaining transparency and traceability of transformations.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The resulting artefact — an edited and enriched dataset — represents data that has been cleansed, quality-checked, and enhanced, ready for statistical estimation or modeling.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Key capabilities: Data Quality Management, Data Editing, Imputation &amp; Derivation, Non-response Correction, Data Validation &amp; Verification."
    viewpoint="value_stream">
